                "headline": "Flash Flood Warning issued September 18 at 9:08AM MDT until September 18 at 12:15PM MDT by NWS Pocatello ID",
                "description": "FFWPIH\n\nThe National Weather Service in Pocatello has issued a\n\n* Flash Flood Warning for...\nThe Ohio burn scar in...\nNorthwestern Blaine County in central Idaho...\n\n* Until 1215 PM MDT.\n\n* At 908 AM MDT, Doppler radar indicated thunderstorms producing\nheavy rain over the Ohio Burn Scar. The expected rainfall rate is\n0.5 to 1 inch in 1 hour. Flash flooding is ongoing or expected to\nbegin shortly. Excessive rainfall over the burn scar will result in\ndebris flow moving through the Ohio burn scar. The debris flow can\nconsist of rock, mud, vegetation and other loose materials.\n\nHAZARD...Life threatening flash flooding. Thunderstorms producing\nflash flooding in and around the Ohio Burn Scar.\n\nSOURCE...Radar indicated.\n\nIMPACT...Life threatening flash flooding of areas in and around the\nOhio Burn Scar.\n\n* Some locations that will experience flash flooding include...\nMainly rural areas of Northwestern Blaine County.",
                "instruction": "This is a life threatening situation. Heavy rainfall will cause\nextensive and severe flash flooding of creeks...streams...and ditches\nin the Ohio Burn Scar. Severe debris flows can also be anticipated\nacross roads. Roads and driveways may be washed away in places. If\nyou encounter flood waters...climb to safety.",
